         <div type="bio">
            <p>Prominent Irish publisher of the literary revival years. Hone co-founded Maunsel &amp; Company in 1905. The firm published a short-lived but influential literary magazine, <hi rend="italic">The Shanachie</hi>, and through 1923 published some 500 titles by major Irish literary figures. From 1909 to 1912, Maunsel was involved in an extended dispute with JJ over the publication of <name type="work" key="W_DUBLINERS">Dubliners</name>, but ultimately backed out of the agreement due to fears of prosecution for obscenity or libel. Hone himself became well-known as a reviewer and later as a biographer. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
